From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lethalbas <lethalbas@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 13:42:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rt(tse,tfe): batch brush polygons per entity; respect RTGL1
 static capacity

TSE 1_2_Palenque in RT logged "Can't find static geometry with unique ID"
/ RG_CANT_UPDATE_TRANSFORM (SceneBrushes.cpp) and then exited or hung.

Cause: brush polygons were batched only while consecutive polygons of one
sector shared the same material state, so the level produced 5127 static
brush geometries (avg ~10 vertices each). RTGL1 has a fixed capacity of
4096 bottom-level geometries in total (static + dynamic per frame); its
VertexCollector::AddGeometry silently rejects anything beyond it and
rgUploadGeometry still returns RG_SUCCESS. Every movable brush part
registered after slot 4096 therefore had no RTGL1 geometry, and the
transform updates failed. Static world geometry beyond the cap was
missing as well, and no slots were left for dynamic geometry.

Fix (root cause): collect the polygons of all active sectors of a brush
entity and group them by the existing batching key (textures, blending,
flags, mask, mirror/warp, media), keeping the polygon order inside a
group. The grouping is deterministic, so the brushPartIndex sequence is
identical in the upload, tex-coord and rasterized passes.
1_2_Palenque: 5127 -> 1405 geometries, same index count.

Mitigation (in addition): SceneBrushes tracks RTGL1's static budget
(geometries with 1024 slots reserved for dynamic geometry, vertices,
indices), does not upload parts that would be dropped, never records
movable IDs or tex-coord parts for parts that were not uploaded, and
prints one console line if parts were dropped.

Same code in the TFE tree (files were identical).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
